<p>
A lore <em>section</em> is just the <code>category</code> field of
<code>config/lore/&lt;code&gt;.json</code>; several texts can share one. The one-line description comes from the
<code>loretype-&lt;category&gt;</code> lang key (BetterRuins authors those as <code>game:loretype-...</code> so
they land in the vanilla namespace). The <code>tapestry</code> and <code>wallcarving</code> files aren't books you
find: they're the chapter collections that tapestries and wallcarvings reveal, so they get their own text
pages under <code>/lore/</code> while everything else lives under <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}sources/books/">Books</a>.
</p>
<p>
A section's "Structures" column is the union of its texts' structures -- see <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}sources/books/">how books are located</a>.
</p>
